                                                                            <comments>
                            <comment id="496335" author="lixi_wc" created="Wed, 17 Jun 2026 23:39:45 +0000">&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dongyang" class="user-hover" rel="dongyang"&gt;dongyang&lt;/a&gt;  Would you please investigate &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="496355" author="dongyang" created="Thu, 18 Jun 2026 11:01:22 +0000">&lt;p&gt;So it looks like ubuntu26 is using dd shipped from uutils, and it's not setting O_APPEND on the fd,&lt;br/&gt;
as a result the offset calculation is off, looks like the dd succeeded appending to the file but it's actually re-writing the first 1M.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
root@ubuntu26:~# dd &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;=/dev/urandom bs=1M count=1 oflag=direct &amp;gt;&amp;gt; /mnt/lustre/testdir/testfile 
1+0 records in
1+0 records out
1048576 bytes (1.0 MB, 1.0 MiB) copied, 0.0310931 s, 34 MB/s

root@ubuntu26:~# gnudd &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;=/dev/urandom bs=1M count=1 oflag=direct &amp;gt;&amp;gt; /mnt/lustre/testdir/testfile 
gnudd: error writing &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;'standard output'&lt;/span&gt;: No data available
1+0 records in
0+0 records out
0 bytes copied, 0.00399544 s, 0.0 kB/s
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;using gnudd is fine.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For now I think on the ubuntu26 test environments we should use gnu coreutils:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
sudo apt-get remove coreutils-from-uutils --allow-remove-essential
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="496415" author="yujian" created="Fri, 19 Jun 2026 04:24:43 +0000">&lt;p&gt;After &lt;a href="https://ime-ddn.atlassian.net/browse/DCO-11530" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;DCO-11530&lt;/a&gt; (ubuntu26 tests VMs should use coreutils-from-gnu) was resolved, sanity-pfl tests passed:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/41a2d825-b6ee-4b69-b6d4-e93785f7d6b9" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/41a2d825-b6ee-4b69-b6d4-e93785f7d6b9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Let's close this ticket.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
